<title>DENMARK: Danish July/August retail sales rise.</title>
<headline>Danish July/August retail sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted retail sales index fell to 109.3 in July and 107.8 in August 1996 from 110.2 in June, the national statistics office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>				    July 96   Aug 96     June 96</p>
<p>  Season adjusted volume     109.3     107.8	110.2</p>
<p>  Food, beverages,tobacco    105.7     105.7	105.8</p>
<p>  Clothing etc.		  108.7     106.5	110.6</p>
<p>  Other consumer goods	 114.6     111.1	116.3</p>
<p>NOTE - 1990 base = 100. The non-seasonally adjusted index for July-August 1996 was on average around 2.8 percent up on the same period in 1995, the statistics office said.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
